+## 1. Exact original failure and investigation
+
+The existing test casts eight rays from `(player.x, 1.4, player.y)` at 45° increments, with a 40-unit maximum range. It recursively raycasts **all world children**, not just walls, and counts a direction only when its **nearest hit is farther than 1 unit**. It does not filter the player rig or perform texture-alpha rejection on billboard intersections. The threshold remains **>=4/8**.
+
+The controlled reproduction used the same slice spawn `(21.5,17.5)` and aim/pitch used by the regression. The Step 1 source was reconstructed and verified against its previously recorded SHA-256: `8de584f24e1291a0b741785a5b56043bb49bf375aa2abdcf73d78e65c1e39dad`.
+
+| Direction | Step 1 nearest hit | Step 2 before fix | Fixed Step 2 |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0° (+X) | Player mesh, 0.285; not counted | Same; fail | Same; not counted |
+| 45° (+X,+Z) | Dead-tree card `(31,29)`, 15.779; pass | No hit; fail | Original tree card restored; pass |
+| 90° (+Z) | Statue card, 10.000; pass | Pass | Pass |
+| 135° (−X,+Z) | Lamp card `(16.5,20.5)`, 5.501; pass | Narrow pole misses ray; fail | Lamp stays 3D; not counted |
+| 180° (−X) | Player mesh, 0.285; not counted | Same; fail | Same; not counted |
+| 225° (−X,−Z) | Terrain wall, 6.364; pass | Pass | Pass |
+| 270° (−Z) | No hit | No hit; fail | No hit |
+| 315° (+X,−Z) | Terrain wall, 7.778; pass | Pass | Pass |
+| **Count** | **5/8** | **3/8** | **4/8** |
+
+The lost hits were the broad rotating card envelopes of one tree and one lamp. Their narrow solid replacements did not intersect those rays. The diagnostic found no moved logical anchors or oversized/invalid bounding volumes responsible for that loss. Enlarging trunks/poles or adding blockers would misrepresent the objects and was not done.
+
+A second concrete geometry defect was identified while examining the kit: the box primitive emitted inward-facing polygons. The sum of face-normal/vertex-position dot products for a centered unit test box was **−24**, becoming **+24** after correcting the winding. This affected solid surface rendering; it is distinct from the two lost broad-card ray intersections. Round primitives were not reversed.
+
+Evidence: [original ray details](step2-occlusion-evidence/diagnosis/rays.json) · [fixed production ray details](step2-occlusion-evidence/targeted-fixed/rays.json).
