+# Step 3 — Phase 2: Alex basic animation
+
+**Date:** 2026-09-20  
+**Result: PASS — 23 targeted automated checks passed, 0 failed.**  
+Main sequence: **19 PASS / 0 FAIL**. Rapid restart/turning supplement: **4 PASS / 0 FAIL**. Source-integrity audit also passed. **No full regression was run.**
+
+## Implemented — Alex only
+
+- Idle breathing/spine and head motion.
+- Walking with alternating articulated legs and arm motion.
+- Running with a quicker step, higher foot clearance and stronger upper-body motion.
+- Smoothed idle/walk/run changes; existing `start` and `stop` overlays are read without changing their state machine.
+- Basic reach-and-return gesture through the **existing generic** `ANIM.play('interact')` state. No new puzzle, item, gameplay-event or input binding.
+- World-space planted foot targets, smooth swing/recovery steps and two-bone leg IK. Only the **visual pelvis** is lowered to maintain leg reach; the gameplay root is not moved by the adapter.
+- Safe animator reset/reuse when the existing player visual is reattached to a rebuilt root.
+
+These are original procedural bone poses on the already-approved Mixamo Remy rig, not imported animation clips. No new external asset or license was needed. The existing temporary casual model, rig, meshes, materials, loader and attribution remain unchanged.
+
+## Integration and ownership
+
+Inspected the existing movement state, `ANIM` pose/state machine and Phase 1 visual adapter before implementation. The smallest integration point is **after the existing player-root/placeholder pose application in `update3D`**.
+
+| Production file | Change |
+|---|---|
+| `chernobyl/assets/alex/alex-animation.js` | New Alex-only skeletal adapter |
+| `chernobyl/assets/alex/alex-visual.js` | Cached animator lifecycle, update forwarding and diagnostic getter |
+| `chernobyl/index.html` | Exactly two inserted lines: local script include and one update call |
+
+The adapter reads actual player displacement and existing animation state. It does not replace the movement controller or write player state, `ANIM`, camera transforms, collision data or the player root. Only Alex's seven skinned meshes have rest-pose frustum culling disabled to avoid animated limbs disappearing from stale bounds.
+
+## Requested verification
+
+| Requirement | Result | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Idle plays when stationary | **PASS** | Spine/head motion detected; settled idle has planted feet |
+| Walk follows walking | **PASS** | Existing walk state, articulated alternating legs |
+| Run follows running | **PASS** | Existing run/sprint state and stronger arm/elbow motion |
+| Smooth transitions without breaking movement | **PASS** | Fixed joint/pelvis limits passed; 465 controller/root/camera frames exactly equal to Phase 1 |
+| Existing camera remains correct | **PASS** | Exact Phase 1 trace equality and all four wall/camera cases |
+| Existing collision remains correct | **PASS** | Four directions blocked without player or camera penetration; blocked travel 0.195833 m, limit 0.21 m |
+| No animation-related runtime/console errors | **PASS** | Zero errors in both targeted suites; zero page errors during captures |
+| No severe foot sliding/floating in tested cases | **PASS** | World-planted stance drift, actual skinned sole samples, restart and turn checks; rendered poses reviewed |
+| Exact existing player root retained | **PASS** | Object identity across each exercise; no animation writes to root transforms |
+| Supported start/stop overlays | **PASS** | Both reach the adapter and settle back to idle |
+| Generic interaction infrastructure | **PASS** | Existing generic interaction reaches and returns without a new gameplay hook |
+
+### Main sequence and fixed limits
+
+The main harness runs identical deterministic input against Phase 1 and the final implementation: **90 idle + 105 walk + 105 run + 90 stop + 75 interaction frames**, at 60 Hz. It then checks four collision directions, read-only state and root rebuilds in outdoor/apartment/slice scenes.
+
+| Measurement | Final observed maximum/minimum | Unchanged acceptance limit |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Single-frame joint rotation | 0.342370743 rad | < 0.4 rad |
+| Single-frame pelvis displacement | 0.036161164 m | < 0.06 m |
+| Planted ankle drift per frame | 0.0000000327 m | < 0.015 m |
+| Ankle-to-IK-target error | 0.0000000860 m | < 0.01 m |
+| Lowest actual skinned sole vertex | −0.000091425 m | ≥ −0.02 m |
+| Maximum absolute contact-sole height | 0.000622270 m | ≤ 0.025 m |
+| Contact samples | 707 | > 100 |
+
+Actual sole geometry was sampled: **965 left / 993 right vertices**, not just IK target positions.
+
+The supplemental checks exercise **nine starting gait timings**, each followed by a two-frame stop, restart, 90° turn and settled idle. All retain the root and finish with planted feet. Maximum joint/pelvis changes remain 0.342371 rad / 0.0361612 m; maximum contact-sole height is 0.000622277 m. These numerical-only cases perform the renderer's scene-matrix update without GPU drawing; rendered inspection is recorded separately.
+
+## Visual inspection
+
+Reviewed the generated pose sheet and real game-camera capture. Idle, start, walk, run, stop, settled idle and interaction are distinct; leg articulation and the reach gesture are visible. No severe foot penetration or implausible whole-body displacement was observed in these sampled views. Continuous motion/foot-contact acceptance is supported by the frame-by-frame measurements above, not by still images alone.
+
+- [Pose inspection sheet](step3-alex-animation-evidence/pose-sheet.png) — inspection camera only, existing scene lighting/materials.
+- [Walking from the existing game camera](step3-alex-animation-evidence/walk-game.png).
+- [Running from the existing game camera](step3-alex-animation-evidence/run-game.png).
+- Individual source frames and capture metadata are in `step3-alex-animation-evidence/`.
+
+## Failures found and resolved
+
+Initial versions of the **new** animation adapter failed the new smoothness check. The first measured maxima were **0.768259 rad / 0.073641 m**. Pelvis reach margins alone did not fix the gait. Later, the new edge cases exposed a rapid-restart/turning problem: phase-only foot timing could hold a foot too long or misclassify an airborne recovery as planted.
+
+The final adapter uses distance-triggered release and timed, predicted landing targets. Airborne recoveries remain airborne until touchdown. The original main harness and all acceptance thresholds were retained; the final runs above passed after those production fixes.
+
+The supplemental harness also had an initial **fixture error**: omitting renderer-driven skinned-mesh matrix updates produced an empty sole sample group. Restoring scene-matrix updates corrected sampling; no assertion or tolerance was removed or weakened. Its invalid first result is retained separately as `edge-fixture-error.json`, not counted as a production result. Earlier production failures remain in `initial-failure.json`, `third-failure.json` and `edge-initial-failure.json`.
+
+## Scope audit — PASS
+
+Compared **825 preexisting files** against hashes saved before this phase:
+
+- Only `chernobyl/index.html` and `chernobyl/assets/alex/alex-visual.js` changed.
+- **No preexisting file is missing.**
+- Removing the two new HTML lines reconstructs the Phase 1 HTML **byte-for-byte**.
+- All Step 2 verification files, assertions, evidence and reports remain unchanged.
+- All Phase 1 evidence, model, local loader and license files remain unchanged.
+- No enemy/Dog/Nika/Subject01 code, puzzles, AI, save/load, lighting, material calibration, world placement, movement/controller or camera math was modified.
+
+Audit: `step3-alex-animation-evidence/scope-verification.json`; exact existing-file edits: `production.diff`.
+
+## Evidence and reproducibility
+
+- `targeted-check.js`, `results.json`, `targeted-check.log`: final **19/0** main run.
+- `edge-check.js`, `edge-results.json`, `edge-check.log`: final **4/0** supplement.
+- `trace.json.gz`: complete baseline/current main-frame telemetry.
+- `phase1-baseline/*.gz`: frozen Phase 1 HTML/visual-adapter sources for the baseline interception.
+- `start-hashes.json`, `scope-verification.json`: pre-phase hashes and final scope audit.
+
+Commands used in this sandbox (server serves `chernobyl/` on port 8000):
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=/home/user/.cache/alex-tools/node_modules \
+LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/tmp/al2023/lib \
+node step3-alex-animation-evidence/targeted-check.js
+
+NODE_PATH=/home/user/.cache/alex-tools/node_modules \
+LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/tmp/al2023/lib \
+node step3-alex-animation-evidence/edge-check.js
+```
+
+The harness uses Puppeteer, `/tmp/chromium` and the cached Phase 1 sources at `/home/user/.cache/alex-animation/`. If that source cache is absent, decompress the two `phase1-baseline/*.gz` files there under their original filenames. These tool dependencies are not production game dependencies.
+
+## Limits / stopping point
+
+This is the requested **basic procedural Alex animation pass**, not a final motion-capture or costume pass. Advanced crouch/injury/death/terrain-specific animations, object-aligned hand contacts and enemy animation are not newly authored or certified here. The checks cover the stated flat-ground sequences at 60 Hz, the tested turns/restarts, collision directions and rebuilds—not every possible terrain/input/frame-rate combination.
+
+One existing Three.js UMD deprecation warning remains informational; it is not an animation/runtime error and no engine migration was attempted.
+
+**Stopped after targeted Alex verification. No full regression run or claim of a new post-animation Step 2 CLEAR.**
