+# Temporary Alex visual: asset provenance and usage
+
+## Human character
+
+- **Character:** Remy, from Adobe Mixamo. This is a temporary visual base, not a final Alex likeness or military/pilot outfit.
+- **Original service:** https://www.mixamo.com/
+- **Exact converted GLB source:** https://github.com/LabMOSA/wheelsims/blob/0bf8b35f3dc43e0066027dff1e593efa643df312/src/objects/humans/bodies/remy/remy.glb
+- **Introducing commit:** https://github.com/LabMOSA/wheelsims/commit/0bf8b35f3dc43e0066027dff1e593efa643df312 — “Added all characters from Mixamo, they are all ready to be used.”
+- **Verified source SHA-256:** `91512558b33f5474bfb60b2e161e7373dd6359217ed73ee6e3253d7b2a562c77`.
+- **Format/exporter:** glTF 2.0 / Khronos glTF Blender I/O v5.0.21. Embedded textures, 7 skinned meshes, 67 joints, 35,196 triangles.
+
+### Permission verified before import
+
+Adobe's official Mixamo FAQ explicitly permits using characters and animations royalty-free in personal, commercial and non-profit projects, including **video games**:
+
+https://helpx.adobe.com/creative-cloud/faq/mixamo-faq.html
+
+Relevant text: “You can use both characters and animations royalty free for personal, commercial, and non-profit projects including: ... Create video games.”
+
+This asset is included solely as an embedded character visual in **CHERNOBYL: ECHOES OF ZERO**. Do not offer it as a standalone character download, resell it, or redistribute it as an asset pack/template. See Adobe's usage clarification:
+
+https://community.adobe.com/t5/mixamo-discussions/mixamo-characters-for-commercial-games/td-p/11815020
+
+**The character is not CC0 or Apache-2.0.** The source repository's Apache license is not treated as a relicensing of Adobe's character content. Any general repository/code license does not override the character's original Mixamo terms.
+
+### Game-local preparation
+
+`remy.glb` retains the original skeleton, joints, inverse bind matrices, weights, geometry, materials and embedded textures. The source animation declaration was removed: no clips are loaded or played. Unreferenced source animation buffer bytes remain to avoid unnecessary binary rewriting; these are not active animation tracks.
+
+The visual adapter applies a one-time arm-rest pose, scales the complete visual to 1.82 world units, aligns its sole/ankle center with the existing player root, and rotates its authored +Z facing to the existing root's −Z convention. None of these transforms writes to the gameplay player or camera.
+
+Casual shirt, shorts and shoes are intentionally retained for this authorized temporary-base phase. Military/pilot clothing, boots, final likeness and animation integration remain future work.
+
+## Loader code
+
+`gltf-loader.js` bundles the **Three.js r160 GLTFLoader and its BufferGeometryUtils dependency** under the MIT license. See `THREE-LICENSE.txt`.
+
+Source: https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/tree/r160/examples/jsm
+
+It uses the game's existing `window.THREE` instance. It does not load another Three.js engine, renderer, framework or CDN. No build tool is required to run the game.
